^.*CONVERSION ERROR.*$
--
[expr.prim.lambda.closure]/1 + §7.5.6.2: a captureless, non-generic lambda is
lowered to a closure class (struct) with operator() (the body) and a
non-explicit conversion to pointer-to-function.  The lambda is usable both as an
object (operator() call, by-value pass/copy, closure-type deduction) and as a
function pointer (via the conversion).  Phase A of
doc/architectural/cpp-lambda-closure-support.md.
